course: dictionary
lesson: 2681
title: Dice: one die, many dice
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A die is one small cube with dots from 1 to 6 on its sides. Two or more are dice. «Roll dice inside the box lid or a tray, so they do not get lost and nobody argues about the number.» Here dice means more than one cube.
explain: Dice is also a verb. To dice food is to cut it into small cubes, as in «dice the carrots». The same word names the cube with dots and the cutting of food into cubes.
explain: Many people in everyday British English say «a dice» for one, but the proper word for one is die. In maths, two dice can give a total from 2 to 12, so dice help you practise adding.
fact: Die is the singular (one) and dice is the plural (more than one).
fact: Dice are small cubes with dots from 1 to 6 on their sides, used in games.
fact: «Dice was first the plural of "die"; today many people also say "a dice" for one.»
fact: Each number on a single die has a chance of 1 in 6.
fact: «In a dice game luck decides, so there is nobody to blame when you lose.»
exercise: What is the plural of die? | Dies | Dicer | *Dice | Diced
exercise: «Dice the carrots.» What does dice mean here? | Cook them whole | Throw them away | Roll them to see the number | *Cut into small cubes
exercise: Two dice are rolled. What is the lowest total you can get? | 6 | 12 | *2 | 1
test: How many faces does one die have? | *6 | 4 | 12 | 8
test: Jayden says «a dice» for one. What is the more correct word for one? | diced | dice | *die | dies
exam: In a dice game, why is there nobody to blame when you lose? | Because you forgot the rules | Because the dice were too small | *Because luck decides the result | Because the other player cheated
